{
  "raw": {
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Multimedia-Content-Creator_JR100361": {
      "title": "Multimedia Content Creator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. Position Summary The Multimedia Content Creator supports marketing objectives by creating multimedia content that captures audiences’ interests, applying technical and creative storytelling skills, and shepherding content creation projects from start to finish. While the primary purpose is development and production of video content, it is also requires a combination of technical knowledge; a working knowledge of graphic communication including video and audio production, multimedia editing, photography skills; the ability to create storytelling scripts and captions; and an understanding of how multimedia is created and formatted for use on social media and websites. This position requires a dynamic, professional, energetic, creative, highly detailed and organized individual who can balance multiple tasks and deadlines in a fast-paced environment.   Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Ideation, planning, scheduling, organizing, and producing content for a variety of platforms, utilizing best practices and techniques. Overseeing production needs, including recording content and setting up lighting and audio engineering; ability to move equipment. Video editing, color correcting, green screening, animations. This position will need to be versed in audio editing software such as Final Cut Pro, Adobe Premier, photo editing programs, and other video/audio tools; Researching and assessing new content production methods and technology, and makes recommendations for new equipment and process enhancements, as appropriate; Placing content on social media channels and the website; Maintaining content library and backups, supplying video footage/content to partnering organizations as needed; Oversee and work with external vendors and student interns/work studies to identify and capture content opportunities. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree or an Associate Degree with significant years of related experience required. At least two years of experience preferred, which can include internship experience. Possess strong creative writing and verbal communication skills. Knowledge of audio, video, graphic and digital production/communication technology Must have advanced computer skills related to digital marketing and multimedia development field such as Final Cut Pro, Adobe Premier, photo editing programs, and other video/audio tools. Working knowledge of web content management systems preferred Familiarity with social media platforms preferred Knowledge and understanding of the College to effectively communicate information about Le Moyne to an internal or external audience. Must demonstrate sensitivity to the importance of Le Moyne’s Jesuit tradition. Possess excellent organizational skills and be attentive to details. Must be self-directed, but a team player and have the ability to work under tight deadlines and on several projects simultaneously. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $30.00 - $33.50 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Occupational-Therapist-and-Community-Program-Leader_JR100347": {
      "title": "Community Health and Wellness Program Leader",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                         The Community Health and Wellness Program Leader is responsible for planning, implementing, and  evaluating community-based programs that promote healthy aging, independence, wellness, and fall  prevention for older adults. This position provides evidence-informed fall prevention programming,  exercise and education, participant screening and functional assessments within the employee's  training and scope of practice, and wellness interventions while collaborating with community  organizations throughout Central New York. The Community Health and Wellness Program Leader  assists with program development, participant outcome measurement, data management, community  outreach, and social media engagement to support CARE's mission of improving the health, safety,  and quality of life of older adults. This is a part time position working 20-25 hours per week. The position includes a combination of in person work at Le Moyne College and community program sites and remote work for appropriate  administrative, planning, data, outreach, and social media responsibilities. This position is funded by external sources and is contingent on the continued receipt of those funds. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Fall Prevention and Community Wellness Deliver CARE fall prevention, healthy aging, wellness, and exercise programming for older adults in community-based settings. Lead group exercise and educational components in a safe, engaging, and age-appropriate manner and adapt activities to participant abilities and established program protocols. Complete participant screenings and standardized functional measures within the employee's  education, credentials, training, and scope of practice; identify concerns that require referral to an  appropriate licensed healthcare professional. Provide education related to fall-risk reduction, home safety, mobility, healthy aging, assistive  devices, caregiver strategies, and other wellness topics consistent with training and professional  scope. Assist with the development and implementation of CARE programs, workshops, presentations,  and community initiatives. Community Partnerships and Outreach Develop and maintain positive working relationships with community partners, older adults,  caregivers, healthcare organizations, and agencies serving older adults. Assist with outreach to identify new program sites, partnership opportunities, presentations,  community events, and referral relationships. Represent CARE and Le Moyne College professionally at community programs, meetings, health  fairs, and outreach events. Social Media and Digital Outreach Assist with and maintain CARE's social media presence as a required responsibility of the position. Create, schedule, and post program updates, educational content, event promotion, participant  highlights, and community outreach content on CARE's approved social media platforms. Assist with basic content creation using Canva or similar tools and coordinate photographs,  graphics, captions, and program information in accordance with CARE and Le Moyne College  policies. Data Management and Program Evaluation Collect, maintain, and assist with analysis of participant and program data, ensuring timely and  accurate entry into required tracking systems. Support outcome measurement and reporting for funders, community partners, and organizational  leadership. Assist with preparation of program metrics, summaries, presentations, and grant-related reports  that demonstrate program reach and impact. Maintain participant confidentiality and follow applicable organizational policies and data-security  practices. General Responsibilities Participate in required meetings, training, and professional development activities. Collaborate effectively with CARE staff, Le Moyne College departments, students, community  partners, and interdisciplinary professionals. Demonstrate professionalism, reliability, sound judgment, initiative, integrity, and respect for the  dignity of all participants. Perform other duties related to CARE programming and community health initiatives as assigned. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Education or professional preparation in a field related to health, rehabilitation, exercise, aging,  wellness, or community health. Appropriate backgrounds may include Occupational Therapy  (OT/OTA), Physical Therapy (PT/PTA), Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Health Promotion, Public  Health, Gerontology, or a closely related field. For applicants working under a licensed or certified healthcare profession, current New York State  licensure/certification and good standing are required when applicable to the duties performed. Demonstrated ability to safely lead or support exercise, wellness, health education, rehabilitation, or community-based programming. Strong communication and interpersonal skills and the ability to work effectively with older adults  and community partners. Comfort with basic technology and digital tools, including Microsoft Office, Zoom, Canva, Instagram, Facebook, and/or similar platforms. Ability and willingness to create and manage social media content as an ongoing responsibility of  the position. Strong organizational skills and ability to work independently in both in-person and remote settings. Reliable transportation and ability to travel to community program sites throughout Central New  York. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with older adults, fall prevention, balance and mobility, community wellness,  rehabilitation, or chronic disease prevention. Experience leading group exercise, health education, workshops, or community-based programs. Experience with program coordination, community outreach, data collection, outcome tracking, or  grant-funded initiatives. Relevant certifications or training in evidence-based fall prevention, older-adult fitness, or wellness  programming are a plus. Physical Requirements The position requires the ability to travel between community sites; stand, walk, demonstrate exercise  and mobility activities, and assist with program setup; and lift/carry program materials and equipment  up to approximately 25 pounds. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified  individuals to perform the essential functions of the position. Work Environment and Schedule Work is performed through a combination of community-based, on-campus, and remote settings. In person programming and travel are essential components of the role. Remote work may be used for  approved administrative tasks, program planning, data entry, outreach, social media, and other duties  that do not require on-site presence. Some schedule flexibility may be required to meet community  program and event needs. Additional Information: Pay Range: $35.00 - $40.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Registrar_JR100359": {
      "title": "Registrar",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Registrar serves as the College’s FERPA Compliance Officer and is responsible for the leadership, management, integrity, and security of all student academic records. The Registrar is entrusted with providing vision, leadership, and management oversight for all administrative functions of the Office of the Registrar, ensuring the integrity, security, and accessibility of student records and academic data. The Registrar leads a dedicated team responsible for oversight of student academic records and registration processes, including the maintenance and long term retention of student academic records; the development of the academic calendar and schedule of classes; classroom assignments; course registration system and processes; the collection and distribution of student grades; the certification of enrollment and degrees; the certification for graduation and preparation of diplomas; the enforcement of academic policies; and the maintenance of basic enrollment and demographic data. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Duties and Responsibilities  Manage all aspects of the College’s Registrar’s Office and student records including, but not limited to, department budget, grading, transfer credit, registration, first-year placements, academic calendars, course scheduling, degree and enrollment certifications, submissions to the National Student Clearinghouse, degree audits, the College’s academic calendar, catalog, and course offerings. Oversee the management of policies, processes, and operations of the College in relation to academic records and student success. Serve as the College’s FERPA Compliance Officer and supervises the protection of student educational records under federal privacy regulations. Motivate and lead a high-performance management team; supervise, train, manage, develop team members. Provide leadership for a complex operation that supports students, faculty, advisors, and others across the institution. Maintain and advocate for the highest level of compliance, integrity, and transparency in all areas, especially for educational information and records. Responsible for NYS Department of Labor ETPL program certifications to support grant funding for student enrollment. Serve as the Custodian of Records for Cazenovia College and other legacy records; overseeing the maintenance and management of transcripts, diplomas, and other student records for the closed college. Maintain and manage our student self-service system in collaboration with Information Technology (IT) with regard to access, training, development and implementation of curriculums, advisor information, and overall utilization. Assist Institutional Research (IR) on providing information related to internal data requests that will not be made external. Collaborate with Information Technology (IT) and college partners to deliver data strategies that foster data literacy and integrity among users to better achieve operational goals, improve efficiencies and help inform strategic decisions. Support the college on accurate and timely responses supporting compliance with federal and state requirements as well as institutional audits. Supervise the Director of Academic Athletic Compliance. Remain current on higher education regulations, accreditation standards, industry best practices, and emerging technologies impacting records and registration services. Manage the registration relationships between partner institutions. Serve as a College representative on college-wide committees as needed.   Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Master’s Degree required; preferred in the areas of High Education, College Student Personnel, Student Affairs Administration, or a related field.  Minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in a registrar's office or related office within higher education (preferred).  Thorough knowledge of FERPA and addressing related concerns with regard to the protection of student educational records. Demonstrated strong knowledge of regulatory, professional, and ethical guidelines in enrollment management to ensure compliance with college, state, federal, and other outside agency rules and regulations. Demonstrated expertise in the use of student information systems (Ellucian Colleague preferred), scheduling software, data reporting tools, and document imaging systems. Strong technical skills. Strong leadership and management skills, with the ability to motivate and inspire staff. Excellent analytical, problem-solving, communication, interpersonal, change-management, and conflict resolution skills. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students. A demonstrated pattern of sound judgment, tact, and the ability to handle confidential and sensitive information appropriately. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $87,000-96,000 Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Assistant-Registrar_JR100358": {
      "title": "Assistant Registrar",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Assistant Registrar is responsible for all functions within the Registrar’s Office as it relates to academic scheduling, classroom management, curriculum management, the College’s academic calendar, as well as the College Catalog. In collaboration with other Assistant/Associate Registrars, this position will support the oversight of operations within the Registrar’s Office to ensure successful and efficient performance.  PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Provide excellent customer service to the constituents of the Registrar’s Office (i.e. students, families, faculty, staff, external agencies, etc.) regarding student records Contribute to the day-to-day operations of the Registrar’s Office as well as campus-wide planning related to long-term classroom utilization strategies and course offerings. Oversees the full scheduling lifecycle, including development and publication of the course schedule, the final exam schedule, and year-round academic calendars ensuring accuracy, consistency, operational efficiency, and compliance with college, state, and federal academic policies and priorities. Generates reports and provides data analysis of current and past semesters to department chairs and deans to aid in the creation of future course schedules, improve classroom utilization, and efficient registration cycles. Allocate classrooms and lecture halls based on enrollment caps, technology needs, and department requests. Identifies and resolves complex scheduling issues, recommends and implements improvements to scheduling practices, and evaluates policies to support effective and equitable use of instructional space. Collaborate with Academic Affairs, faculty leadership, and governance bodies to implement approved curriculum changes, academic policies, program requirements, and catalog updates within university systems. In collaboration with the Curriculum Committee Chair, critically reviews submissions for accuracy to determine appropriateness of requested changes and assists in the resolution of any issues. Serve on the Academic Calendar Committee and collaborates with the Associate Provost to create all academic calendars and ensure that Middle States and New York State Department of Education requirements regarding instruction time are met. Create the initial draft of forthcoming academic year(s) calendars for review by the Committee. Maintenance of document management and workflow solutions, including OnBase, Google forms, and related technologies. Assist the Registrar’s Office with: All communications to and from the Registrar’s office, including phone calls, emails, and official correspondences. Maintenance of student educational records. The identification, investigation and resolution of issues and processing errors regarding registration and records areas. Streamlining policies and procedures to improve efficiency. Evaluate, implement, and test new software, upgrades, and new systems utilized in the Registrar’s Office. Development of training materials and serve as the College’s training resource for best practices within student information systems, supportive software, reporting, and solutions for student information systems (SIS) and related software. Serve on selected college committees. Attendance at College events as needed (some evenings and weekends). Other duties as assigned. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree and 2-5 years of related experience in a higher education setting (experience in a Registrar’s Office is preferred). Professional demeanor and ability to interact well with others in a fast-paced operation. Strong knowledge of student records administration, academic operations, and higher education business processes. Demonstrated ability to analyze complex issues, develop practical solutions, and lead operational improvements. Strong interpersonal, leadership, communication, and organizational skills as well as proven ability to work collaboratively. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines effectively. Attention to detail and proficiency in Excel is essential. Respect for confidential information; working knowledge of FERPA is required. Experience with Colleague Datatel, Unity OnBase, Parchment, AdAstra, and Informer is preferred. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $62,354 - $63,300 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Pep-Band-Director-Instructor_JR100343": {
      "title": "Pep Band Director/Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                   The Director of the Pep Band is a part-time position that is vital to creating the spirited, energetic atmosphere that defines Le Moyne's athletic events - especially at home men's and women's basketball games and other major college functions. Post-season travel is to be expected in the event that any college team is selected for conference and NCAA tournaments. The Director will play a key role in fostering a welcoming and inclusive environment for student musicians, ensuring that all members feel valued and supported in their musical and personal growth. This is a part time 12-month position with primary reporting to the Music Program Director and secondary reporting to the Athletics Director/AVP, Intercollegiate Athletics and Recreation. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Performances & Appearances: Attend, direct, and facilitate Pep Band performances and appearances. Collaborate with Athletics and Spirit Squad staff on performance logistics. Coordinate transportation, setup, and other logistical needs for performances. Promote the Pep Band through campus engagement and marketing initiatives. Foster a sense of community and school spirit among student musicians. Practice & Rehearsals: Schedule and conduct rehearsals (minimum of one per week) to prepare the Pep Band for performances. Administrative Responsibilities & Scheduling: Oversee Pep Band member participation, scheduling, and engagement, in close collaboration with Athletics and other College offices. Communicate and coordinate with the music program as appropriate. Maintenance & Inventory: Manage and maintain instruments, equipment, and uniforms. Performance & Safety: Support the safety and well-being of all Pep Band members during practices, travel, and performances. Collaborate with Le Moyne staff to prepare emergency response plans aligned with college protocols. Follow guidance provided by Le Moyne Sports Medicine and relevant departments. Music Instructor Requirement to instruct one section of MUS 395 (1-credit course) per Fall and Spring semester. All Pep Band members who are Le Moyne College students will be required to register for this course each semester of their involvement. Additional Responsibilities Maintain active and positive relationships with area high school band directors and others within the recruiting region Initial recruitment goals are 10-15 new students each fall with an annual ensemble enrollment of 30 plus students. Cultivate positive alumni and community relationships Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Master's degree in Music, Education, or a related field required. Experience leading a band or similar ensemble, preferably at the collegiate or high school level. Strong musical leadership skills. Excellent communication, organization, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and during game-day events. Familiarity with drumline instruction and coordination, particularly in a marching or athletic band setting; ability to integrate percussion effectively into high-energy performances is strongly preferred. Additional Information: Pay Range: $15,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Assistant-Coach--Men-s-and-Women-s-Swimming-and-Diving-and-Assistant-Director--Aquatics_JR100360-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Swimming and Diving and Assistant Director, Aquatics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Assistant Coach for Men and Women’s Swimming and Diving responsible for providing assistance and support for the conduct of a comprehensive, high quality NCAA Division I men’s and women’s swimming programs, within the guidelines of all rules and policies established by the department, the institution, the NEC Conference, and the NCAA, in accordance with the academic standards, and the stated mission of Le Moyne College and the Athletic Department, including the advancement of its “Inside the L“ shared culture. This position will require daily and/or weekly duties and tasks as assigned by the head coach which require exercising discretion and independent judgment consisting of 75% instructional and 25% recruitment/administrative activities. This position will also serve as the Assistant Director of Aquatics. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: NCAA Compliance Assist program in compliance with all applicable NCAA, conference, and institutional policies, rules and regulations. Assist with timely submission of all compliance related work flows through ARMS to maintain the highest levels of integrity and transparency. Maintain open and responsive communications with the Associate Director of Compliance Maintain up to date certification in all required areas (NCAA DI Institute Modules, 1st Aid/CPR/AED Training, Etc). Fiscal Management Assist the Head Coach with the submission of budget requests, documentation, receipts, and related forms as assigned. These requests must be submitted promptly in accordance with existing College Wide policy. Enrollment Management Assist leading and supporting the College Enrollment Management priorities through partnership, participation, and meeting goals with Enrollment Management initiatives as assigned by head coach. Assist the department with its gender equity planning and the satisfaction of all Title IX legislation by striving to attain goals related to any applicable enrollment management initiatives within your particular program as assigned by head coach. Assist head coach with responding to all requests for information from prospective student-athletes, coaches, parents, and/or friends of prospective student-athletes. Assist head coach with solicit information from and distribute information to eligible prospective student-athletes and coaches and or parents or friends of prospective student-athletes. Assist head coach with developing and distributing appropriate recruiting materials, publications and information to interested prospective student-athletes. Assist head coach with maintaining accurate and comprehensive recruiting records of all prospective student athletes. College and Department Service It is expected that employees have a willingness and commitment to be broadly engaged and in service to the College as demonstrated through participation on committees and attendance at College functions/events. It is expected that employees participate with department committees, as elected or assigned, to develop, evaluate and enhance department policy. Attendance at all departmental meetings, unless excused in advance by the AVP for Athletics, is expected while a commitment to the College's priorities and the department's goals and objectives are vital to the success of the position. Academic Support Assist head coach with providing the appropriate academic support, assistance, motivation and environment for student-athletes. Become familiar with appropriate academic resource and assistance programs available to student-athletes. Assist head coach with monitoring the academic progress of your student-athletes from current class work to graduation. Understand current institutional academic standards and policies. Game Management Assist head coach with working with appropriate personnel to determine your needs for the organization, coordination, and scheduling of all home and away contests including:  facility and equipment set-up, officials, scorekeepers, statisticians, media considerations, lodging, meals, travel arrangements, etc. Swim Meet Management Assist head coach with working with appropriate personnel to determine your needs for the organization, coordination, and scheduling of all home and away contests including:  facility and equipment set-up, officials, timing table, statisticians, media considerations, lodging, meals, travel arrangements, etc. Sports Performance Submit all paperwork, schedule meetings and respond to all information requests from athletic trainers and team physicians according to guidelines and deadlines established by the Head Athletic Trainer as assigned by head coach. All decisions regarding the health and safety of student athletes when it comes to physical participation is at the discretion of the Head Athletic Trainer. Assist head coach with coordinating with Head Strength/Conditioning Coach on the conduct of a comprehensive training program to enhance both personal and performance growth/development. Sports Information Respond to all information requests and work with the media, etc. according to guidelines and deadlines established by the Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Communications as assigned by head coach. Always inform the Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Communications when you or any of your athletes has been contacted by the media. Facility Management & Assistant Director of Aquatics Ensure proper maintenance of the Ryan Aquatic Center Collaborate with Physical Plant for repairs and upkeep Follow all State and Local guidelines for monitoring of water quality Schedule and manage external rentals for pool use Communicate with Director of Aquatics issues that arise with facility Fund Raising Assist head coach with fund raising activities. Particular attention should be given to NCAA legislation surrounding booster groups and donors. Reconciliation of all revenues and deposits should be handled in accordance with institutional and departmental policy. Community Service A commitment to community services is an important tenant of the College's mission and to that end it is anticipated that employees will be involved in various community activities as a representative of the Le Moyne College Athletics Department. Assist head coach with identifying and cultivating a community partnership with a service-based organization to provide an impactful service experience for your student-athletes. Professional Development Opportunities to maintain and advance current understandings of techniques, strategies, theories, and regulations as they relate to the athletics industry are essential. Attendance and participation in conferences is strongly encouraged if assigned by head coach. Supervisory Relationships For purpose of performance evaluations and most other official duties, the first level of contact for the Assistant Coach is with the Head Coach. Appeals of decisions are to be taken to the Director of Athletics. Functional Relationships/Secondary Sources: All coaches are expected to work cooperatively with all members of the Athletic Department (Administrators, Support Staff, Colleagues), and any other campus (admissions, housing, financial aid, maintenance, etc), or community office/agency that you might be involved with. Communications and required documentation should be handled in a timely manner. Camps and Clinics Work with Head Coach on camps and clinics through-out the year. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree required, Master’s Degree in relevant field preferred 1 to 2 years of progressive experience in swim coaching required, 1 to 2 years of progressive experience in the conduct of a collegiate level men’s and women’s swimming and diving programs with proven success in recruiting high quality student athletes and/or equivalent related experiences preferred 1 to 2 years of aquatic facility management including lifeguard staff preferred Knowledge of and ability to apply NCAA and NEC conference rules as they pertain to the men’s and women’s swimming and diving programs. The successful candidate will be required to be First Aid/CPR/AED and Lifeguard certified and to complete all required NCAA DI Institute modules prior to being able to participate in off campus recruiting activities and countable athletically related activities. Working Knowledge of Team Manager and Meet Manager Certified Pool Operator (or acquire with-in 30 days of employment) CPR/AED and Lifeguard Trainer Certification (or acquire with in 6 months) Excellent leadership, organizational, interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills needed. Ability to work off hours, holidays and weekends Ability to travel for recruiting, swim meets and training trips Valid New York State driver’s license (or acquire with-in 30 days of employment) Comfortability with Various social media platforms Understanding of USA Swimming reporting website preferred Previous experience as a collegiate swimmer preferred Working knowledge of ARMS/Teamworks and Workday platforms preferred Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $45,000-49,000 Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Club-Coach--Men-s-Lacrosse_JR100356": {
      "title": "Club Coach, Men's Lacrosse",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Men’s Lacrosse Club Coach is responsible for developing and supporting the Men’s Lacrosse Club program and work with students of different levels of expertise. This position will teach, coach, train and motivate student-athletes to perform at the highest level through organized team and individual sessions. This is a part time exempt position working January through May. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Conduct safe and organized practice sessions/classes and game play oversite that will enable club members to develop and improve their skills Coordinating and supervising all games, practices, off season programs and scheduling Scouting and recruiting prospective student-athletes Ensure that the program complies with all College, Club Sport, Governing Body and Recreational Athletics rules and regulations. Organizes and administers all pre-season, in-season, and post-season activities necessary for team success Foster an environment within the Club program that supports the department mission of personal growth and integrity, diversity, leadership, sportsmanship, and a commitment to athletic and academic excellence. Monitoring team expenses and budgets Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree preferred. 1 to 2 years of experience in Lacrosse and/or equivalent related experiences. Knowledge of league rules and requirements as they pertain to the club sport. The successful candidate will be required to be First Aid/CPR/AED certified. Understanding of budget issues and funds management Excellent leadership, organizational, interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills needed. Working Conditions and Physical Demands Our campus thrives on the energy, collaboration, and shared ideas of our community. We believe that the best student mentorship, professional growth, and creative breakthroughs happen through real-time, face-to-face connection. To support this vibrant academic environment, positions at Le Moyne College are based on-campus. This ensures our teams can seamlessly collaborate, build strong professional relationships, and directly contribute to our student-centered mission. Additional Information: Pay Range:  Stipend $2,500 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
