    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Counselor--Mental-Health_JR100354": {
      "title": "Counselor, Mental Health",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Mental Health Counselor and Outreach Coordinator has the primary responsibility for direct mental health counseling services (diagnostic, assessment, crisis intervention and brief psychotherapy) to all Le Moyne College students but will maintain a specific focus on working with historically underrepresented students and first-generation students. This involves a focus on providing culturally responsive care and will collaborate with campus and community partners to engage in meaningful advocacy, psycho-educational outreach, and clinical intervention designed to promote student success and well-being interventions. This position will be responsible to provide leadership in the ongoing development and implementation of culturally inclusive and innovative mental health outreach to all students.  This is a full time 10-month position with an annual work period of 8/16-6/15. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Provide individual, and group psychotherapy to a broad range of students from undergraduate, graduate, and non-traditional student populations Provide crisis intervention to students experiencing emotional crisis Provide emergency on-call services to students in crisis and/or consultation with other college personnel on a rotating basis Provide case management, collaboration with key personnel, and continuity of care, including referrals to community providers Develop and initiate culturally sensitive outreach, prevention and wellness programming for a diverse range of student concerns and issues  Develop and initiate education and training programs for faculty, staff, and administrators as partners in the wellbeing of all students Provides a level of engagement in working with historically underrepresented students towards their personal development, well-being, and academic success, through culturally responsive individual, group and community. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Masters’ degree in Mental Health or Social work or Doctoral degree in Clinical or Counseling Psychology or Counselor Education, from a CACREP or APA accredited program, or closely related field. License (or license eligible within 6 months) to practice mental health in New York State required. Minimum of 1-3 years of experience providing direct mental health services Experience providing crisis intervention services Experience in providing brief, solution focused psychotherapy Experience in working with historically marginalized populations through culturally responsive individual, group and community interventions Experience in providing educational programming to large groups Clinical experience in a college counseling center setting is strongly preferred A holistic, wellness philosophy and approach is preferred Working Conditions and Physical Demands Our campus thrives on the energy, collaboration, and shared ideas of our community. We believe that the best student mentorship, professional growth, and creative breakthroughs happen through real-time, face-to-face connection. To support this vibrant academic environment, positions at Le Moyne College are based on-campus. This ensures our teams can seamlessly collaborate, build strong professional relationships, and directly contribute to our student-centered mission. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $50,000 - $57,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Coordinator--Clinical-Program-Administration_JR100357": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Clinical Program Administration",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. Position Summary                                                                         The Department of Physician Assistant Studies Program Coordinator is a multifaceted role central to the department’s success, providing critical support and collaboration to the Program Director, Data Analyst, Clinical Team and Didactic and Clinical Year students.  The Program Coordinator establishes open lines of communication with external partners such as sites and preceptors as well as the internal partners that are instrumental to event planning and payment processing. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Administrative Utilize the Workday platform and legacy systems to handle fiscal transactions; support faculty and staff in their use of these platforms and systems Lead collaboration among Program Director, Department Members, Catering, Communications, Facilities, A/V, and external vendors to plan and prepare for major and quotidian department events, at discretion of program director Support special projects and committees, at discretion of program director Coordinate annual student honor society and scholarship awards Serve on college commencement committee; oversee completion of graduation application and ordering of white coats; send congratulatory PANCE cards Address faculty and student needs and triage individuals to the right person/place if unable to meet the faculty member’s or student's needs Maintain OnBase database; upload and retrieve documents as needed Register students for courses and process advisor assignments; interface with the registrar Register/update students in databases for NYSSPA and AAPA Troubleshoot ID card access issues Coordinate lab repairs and maintain office supplies Solicit support from IT and external vendors as needed Draft, review, and send correspondence Maintain procedures manual for administrative responsibilities Clinical Site Management Manage clinical placement lists and updates lists in the ARC-PA portal biannually. Generates reports for the clinical coordinator, Data analyst and program director as requested for ongoing programmatic self-study. Manage AAPA CME credits for PA-C preceptors; prepare report at conclusion of “year” and submit new applications as needed Manage stipends for precepting: request and process W-9s as needed; communicate with Finance and Program Director to ensure payment of stipends. Email student evaluations of preceptors to preceptors annually Verify preceptors performing student evaluations meet ARC-PA standards. Collects and maintains documentation of preceptor licensure, certifications as required by ARC-PA. Review and manage the Exxat webpage; maintain the preceptor website within the placement system Organize and provide Preceptor Placement Report to the Data Analyst and clinical faculty prior to each clinical rotation. Update, set up and publish Learning Activities, Student Profile and Compliance sections in Exxat, our clinical scheduling system. Confirm current affiliation agreement on file for each clinical rotation and preceptor prior to student beginning rotation. Database Maintenance Compile data into Excel spreadsheets, Google Drive and databases as required by internal stakeholders. Ensure Exxat is up-to-date: Maintain, reviews and updates data clinical site requirements, preceptor and staff information and student compliance documents including annual health updates. Maintain Resources section in Exxat. Create rotation-related reports via Exxat. Work in collaboration with Clinical Team to analyze Trends and generate suggestions for improvements. Ensure data is stored appropriately and protected from unauthorized access, and that privacy and security standards are met. Identify and fix errors and inconsistencies in databases to make them more accurate and reliable. Regularly participate in Exxat webinars to enhance understanding of platform; disseminate pertinent information to department members Identify scheduling system issues and provide technical support; serve as the liaison between DPAS and Exxat IT Support. Student Transitions Hold individual meetings with students early in first year to review required documents Collaborate with the clinical team during transition from first to second year. Present Exxat system onboarding to first-year students. Maintain PowerPoint slides and Word documents to help students learn how to navigate Exxat and compliance Manage background check process for clinical year students Register/update students in databases for PAEA, ROSH Review/PANCE prep tools and other external vendor tools to support student learning. Manage PAEA Exam Box registration. Provide face-to-face as well as virtual guidance to answer questions regarding paperwork upload, understanding site requirements, and preparing necessary health documents. Provide excellent customer service to students by relating program information and resources; work to ensure students are held accountable while also feeling supported and set up for success   Additional Duties: Facilitate group interview sessions during the admission process; actively contribute to the development of the group interview case, rubric, script, and flow Maintain procedures manual for clinical responsibilities Assists with Commencement, Transition White Coat Ceremony, White Coat Ceremony, Orientation  Serve on DPAS committee based on program needs and in alignment with professional skills and departmental responsibilities Support grant team as needed; maintain Constant Contact and help transition Project Manager As available and needed, support administrative aspects of mask fit testing, which would occur outside of regular work hours Participate in monthly department meetings and sites/placements meetings Serve on DPAS committee based on program needs and in alignment with professional skills and departmental responsibilities Follow FERPA regulations in maintaining confidential student information. Provides excellent customer service to students by relating program information and resources. Understand and partner with the College’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion to ensure these values are maintained throughout programming and daily interactions. Apply knowledge of administrative and academic operating policies to support student success. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Required: Bachelor’s degree required Demonstrated ability to work independently with problem-solving and conceptual skills. Highly organized self-starter with excellent time-management, problem-solving, and conceptual skills Excellent attention to detail, communication, writing, and interpersonal skills. Ability to efficiently prioritize workload and successfully meet deadlines in an environment with competing priorities Proficient in the use of Google Suite, Microsoft Suite, Canvas, and Zoom. Familiarity with Workday, Exxat, and OnBase systems, preferred, OR adaptable to new platforms Experience creating reports and drafting correspondence with time sensitive data. Proven ability to manage highly sensitive and confidential data with strict adherence to privacy standards. A proactive mindset focused on identifying operational inefficiencies and implementing streamlined process improvements. A positive, collaborative disposition to foster healthy workplace morale and team cohesion. Preferred: ·         2+ years administrative work experience in a higher education environment·         Prior payment processing experience·         Prior event planning experience·         Prior supervisory experience Working Conditions and Physical Demands Our campus thrives on the energy, collaboration, and shared ideas of our community. We believe that the best student mentorship, professional growth, and creative breakthroughs happen through real-time, face-to-face connection. To support this vibrant academic environment, positions at Le Moyne College are based on-campus. This ensures our teams can seamlessly collaborate, build strong professional relationships, and directly contribute to our student-centered mission. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $25.00 - $28.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Security-Officer--4pm-12am_JR100335": {
      "title": "Security Officer, 4pm-12am",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. Job Description: Security Officers are tasked with the general responsibility of the safety and security of the Le Moyne College Campus and Le Moyne College Community. They are service driven and provide both general and emergency public safety/security services. Job duties specific to this position:   Conduct patrols of the campus, which can be walking, fixed post or by vehicle. Provide security services to specific areas of campus as assigned.  Develop and improve working relationships with students, faculty, and staff. Perform some traditional law enforcement duties typically assigned to security personnel.  Respond promptly and professionally to requests for service from students, employees and visitors for emergencies and general security services on campus. Enforce Le Moyne College's rules, regulations and policies. Ensure local, state and federal laws and ordinances are enforced to protect students, faculty/staff and visitors to the campus. Conduct thorough security checks of your assigned areas and report any security or safety issues which could lead to injury or safety concerns in order to ensure their integrity and the safety of their inhabitants and contents.  As assigned - conduct investigations and inquiry into incidents involving violations of College policy, criminal offenses or suspicious circumstances. Submit comprehensive written reports on all such incidents.  Promptly correct and/or report to the appropriate College office all observed safety, security, utility, environmental and fire hazards.  Lock and unlock buildings and rooms as scheduled.  Provide unlocks and lock-ups as requested (i.e., student key ins, office key ins). Conduct monthly inspections of fire extinguishers located on campus.  Stay well informed on all College activity.  Promote crime prevention and fire safety. Maintain a professional appearance to include uniforms, vehicles and personal hygiene. Maintain a level of physical fitness necessary to perform the principle job functions. Perform all related security services or emergency/general duties as requested by the Director of Security or his designee. Maintain a lost and found property. Cover the dispatch desk and duties when assigned. Participate in all required and assigned trainings. Work events as assigned. Test Blue light phones. Provide various forms of transports/escorts. Conduct fire drills. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne's mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college's strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne's established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Requirements: High School Diploma or GED Valid New York State driver's license and a driving record which is aligned with the College's motor vehicle policy Meet and maintain the requirements and training to be licensed and registered as a security guard in New York State. Capable of working evenings, nights, weekends, holidays and in inclement weather. Must be able and willing to work overtime coverage when necessary or directed, including mandatory overtime and for extracurricular campus events.  Strong written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills. Excellent customer service skills The ability to interact in a sensitive, courteous and understanding way with members of a diverse residential and academic community and the general public.  Ability to multi task and to maintain composure in emergency situations.   Ability to respond to calls for service.  Be reliable and able to work independently.  Must exercise good judgment and display sensitivity to the unique role that security plays in a college setting. Able to perform the physical duties of the job including, but not limited to, climbing stairs, crouching, walking, standing, or sitting for extended periods.  Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  40 hour work week Pay Range : $26.30 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace.  We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/HVAC-Mechanic_JR100316": {
      "title": "HVAC Mechanic",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary The HVAC Mechanic is responsible for the repair, maintenance, operation, adjustment and installation of heating, air conditioning, refrigeration equipment, and related control systems. Principal Duties and Essential Functions: Install, repair, adjust, service and maintain electric or pneumatic control systems for heating, ventilation, air conditioning, humidity, laboratory equipment, including calibration of related instruments, gauges and controls. Install, operate, service, and repair conventional mechanical refrigeration/air conditioning equipment including standard refrigerators, and general air conditioning units. Repair, clean, adjust, and/or install oil and gas burners and auxiliary heating specialties other than high-pressure equipment. Conduct necessary tests of equipment to determine malfunctions or causes of breakdown; remove and replace faulty parts, subassemblies and major components; re-test equipment with repaired components and make required adjustments and corrections. Recommend ordering of necessary parts and supplies for maintenance of equipment. Maintain air compressors, air dryers, and low voltage installations such as warning light systems. Instruct and advise users of proper operation of equipment. May be required to make emergency repairs at hours other than normal schedule. May direct helpers and other tradesmen in performance of duties. Calibrate gas ovens and electric grills. Install additional electrical/plumbing components to improve performance or for adaptation of existing systems. Perform duties outside classification incidental to the responsibilities of the Physical Plant Department or such duties assigned. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications: High School diploma or equivalent. Five years minimum experience in HVAC trade with working knowledge of steam hydronic and forced air heating, refrigeration, gas electric, pneumatic and direct digital control systems. Knowledge of heating, refrigeration/air conditioning equipment and/or pneumatic and electrical control systems as applicable to work specialty. Experience with steam, hot water and chilled water systems. Provides their own tools, and knows materials, methods and hazards of trade. Skill in the use of tools of the trade. Sufficient strength and physical dexterity to perform duties and responsibilities of this job, including heavy lifting. Must possess a valid NYS Driver’s license. EPA certification for Refrigerant Handling. May have to work overtime hours on an intermittent basis when operational needs arise . Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  40 hour work week Pay Range:  $28.82 - $30.81 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Administrator--Desktop-Systems_JR100252": {
      "title": "Administrator, Desktop Systems",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Desktop Systems Administrator is responsible and accountable for the effective lifecycle management of Le Moyne’s personal and mobile computing devices, and academic software. This includes processes and technologies associated with acquisition, inventory and asset management, imaging and installation, configuration, maintenance, renewal and disposal of computing devices and software. The Desktop Administrator supervises and coordinates the activities of student employees who support the lifecycle management activities. Actively advances and promotes Le Moyne’s mission, Catholic and Jesuit identity, and commitment to both social justice and care for the whole person PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Desktop Administration Actively leads the lifecycle management of Le Moyne’s personal and mobile computing devices, including device acquisition, creation of OS image and deployment of baseline system configuration, for Windows, Apple Mac OS, Google Chromebook and Apple iOS devices. Ensures timely and consistent distribution of software updates and security patches in accordance with departmental standards. Identifies, utilizes and maintains methods and technologies to promote efficient device and software configuration management. Effectively integrates third party hardware (e.g. printers, scanners, copiers) into Le Moyne’s personal and mobile computing environment. Establishes and documents best practices for the technical support of computing and mobile devices. Evaluates and recommends devices and software to satisfy specified requirements. Serves as a consultant regarding questions involving system(s) installation, configuration, and maintenance. Application Administration Actively leads the end to end lifecycle management of Le Moyne’s academic software, including evaluation, testing, virtualization, distribution, and support across Windows, Apple Mac OS, Google Chromebook and Apple iOS devices. Utilizes established tools to manage the virtualization and distribution of assigned applications. Routinely audits the application portfolio to identify underutilized software for removal, and monitors applications for software updates. Establishes documentation surrounding application management and practices. Serves as a consultant regarding questions involving software installation, configuration, and maintenance. Student Management Serve as primary professional staff member responsible for hiring, training, mentoring, and supervising approximately 10 student staff. Assist in the development of a comprehensive training program to educate Systems and Network Services student staff. Approves timesheets and absences for direct report(s) using the established systems. Schedules appropriate student staffing to support SNS team needs. General Duties At all times, applies principles and practices that promote the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of Le Moyne’s information and information and technology services. Supports the resolution of technology issues. Ensures that assigned incidents and requests are responded to and resolved in accordance with established standards. Collaborates on the maintenance and renewal of systems and software configuration management tools. Collaborates with other IT staff and Le Moyne community members on assigned projects. Communicates effectively in visual, oral, and written form with key constituencies. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Maintains a constituent centric approach at all times. Demonstrates professionalism in contacts with others. Engages in on-call and weekend support. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree or equivalent academic preparation from a regionally accredited college. 1-3 years of relevant experience supporting desktop, software, and mobile computing systems. Successful, prior supervisory and/or team leadership experience in a professional work environment. Proficiency in Microsoft Windows 11, Active Directory, Group Policy, Windows registry, Windows File and Print Services Working experience with Windows server operating systems Proficiency in GSuite, Microsoft Office, Adobe Creative Cloud, and similar productivity tools. Experience in application distribution and virtualization platforms such as AppsAnywhere (or similar management tool) to provide software access. Hands-on experience in configuring SCCM (or similar configuration management tool) to build, deploy and manage PC images Hands-on experience with Jamf (or similar configuration management tool) to build, deploy and manage Mac OS images Experience supporting virtual desktop technologies. Familiar with ITIL (or related) service management practices including incident, problem, configuration, and change management Superior commitment to serving others with empathy, timeliness, accuracy, thoroughness, and professionalism Creative and critical thinker with an open and collaborative style that engenders trust from the College community. Outstanding interpersonal and communication skills; works effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Self-motivated and proactive; works effectively with limited oversight and direction; attentive to detail; organized; ably manages resources, constituencies, projects of varying size, and multiple and competing priorities and deadlines Familiarity with the academic and administrative functions of a college is desirable. TECHNICAL ENVIRONMENT Windows 11, Active Directory, Group Policy, Windows Registry, Window File and Print Apple MacOS and iOS VMware Horizon View, vCenter Google GSuite for EDU, ChromeOS Microsoft SCCM, InTune Microsoft Office, Adobe Creative Suite Software2 AppsAnywhere Desktop Firewall, Anti-Malware Powershell Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  Pay Range: $25.50 - $27.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
