    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Campus-Ministry--Retreat-Ministry-and-Faith-Formation_JR100330": {
      "title": "Campus Ministry, Retreat Ministry and Faith Formation",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-31\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Campus Ministry The Office of Campus Ministry provides opportunities for students, staff, and faculty to grow spiritually, to engage in local, domestic, and international service and social justice opportunities, to make spiritual retreats, reflect on contemporary social issues and to actively practice their faith. Campus Ministry welcomes and serves persons of all religious affiliations and faith traditions. Position Summary                                                                            Under the supervision of the Director of The Grace Center for Faith and Community and in collaboration with the Campus Ministry Staff, the Campus Minister for Retreat Ministry and Faith Formation promotes the deepening of an active faith and spiritual life, personal and communal, among the students of Le Moyne College. The primary ministry is to create vibrant programing, robust retreat offerings, individual and communal prayer/discernment opportunities, and community centered activities that help deepen, renew, or begin a personal relationship with God. This work is accomplished through a strong understanding of Ignatian spirituality and the stages of faith formation in young adults. This position requires a person who will creatively and strategically develop new programs/mediums and refine existing programs based on the ongoing assessment of student needs and interests. This is an 11 month position that works from August through June.   Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Create a compelling vision for and develop a dynamic portfolio of retreats and other experiences which will engage students in various aspects of faith formation and spiritual development.  Implement all aspects of the retreat program and other faith formation opportunities for students based on class year (First Year Student Retreat, Senior Retreat etc.) as well as topic based (Kairos, Busy Student Retreat, Health & Wellness Retreat, Silent Retreat).  Create new retreat and faith formation opportunities for students of all faiths and for those with no religious beliefs.  Promote opportunities to learn about and practice Ignatian Spirituality.  Create and maintain assessment measures for the program.  Recruit, mentor, develop and empower student leaders who support the retreat program.      Reserve and coordinate the use of various retreat facilities and college vans. Coordinate the OCIA & Confirmation program. Work with faith and service-based student organizations. Keep and maintain accurate budget records for all programs. Maintain a respectful environment for a diverse population of students; embrace diversity in the College and greater community, and treat students as individuals. Work collaboratively with the Grace Center team and campus partners Serve, as needed, as a mentor for Campus Ministry's Service opportunities Assist with local service/outreach initiatives. Serve as a Campus Ministry presence at Sunday Mass and attend all special liturgies of the college. Attend and be visible at various religious services on campus, including but not limited to weekly Jumu'ah prayer and Protestant worship. Attending and being visible at various campus events, including but not limited to sporting, musical, lectures, and other social events. Contribute to Mission Integration divisional meetings, webinars and committees Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Master's degree preferred, Bachelor's Degree required in Pastoral Studies, theology or a related field. An understanding of the principles of Ignatian spirituality, the Spiritual Exercises of St. Ignatius, the mission of Jesuit education, and Catholic Social Teaching. Desire to work with a diverse faith community of undergraduate college students. Familiarity with Karios retreat program. Knowledge of O.C.I.A. High level of initiative and imagination. Flexibility to work extended and/or off-hours to meet program needs. Ability to relate and collaborate with various groups both within the Le Moyne College community and the larger Syracuse community. Ability to maintain confidentiality, be self-directed and motivated, possess a high energy level and positive attitude. Knowledge of computers, emphasis on Microsoft Office, Excel, Gmail and various social media platforms. Strong organization and administrative skills. Excellent written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $ 57,158 - $59,500 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Senior-Admission-Couselor_JR100327": {
      "title": "Senior Admission Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Admission Counselor is responsible to educate incoming freshman, transfers, parents and counselors about Le Moyne College and the overall college admission process and manage all aspects of college admission including recruitment, counseling, academic advising and evaluation of prospective students and applicants. This position is based at Le Moyne College in Syracuse, NY with a main recruitment territory of Metro NY. This position requires travel to the Metro NY area for student recruitment.  Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Contribute to the design, development and execution of marketing and recruitment strategies to drive enrollment growth by collaborating with the Director and admission team.  Successfully manage assigned primary, secondary and tertiary geographic territories, conducting extensive travel to build pipelines, lead recruitment events and expand institutional reach.   Counsel, advise and interview prospective first-year and transfer students to guide them through the enrollment lifecycle. Evaluate prospective students’ application materials for final recommendations on admission decisions. Engage in targeted telemarketing and outreach activities to prospective students and applicants. Assist in the coordination and execution of campus open house recruitment events. Plan and host on campus programs for specific student demographics. Maximizes opportunities regarding the college admission process and access to Le Moyne College by delivering inclusive, culturally sensitive guidance to diverse students, parents and counselors. Plans travel and recruitment in the Metro NY area: Visit high schools, junior colleges and multicultural agencies to educate students and counselors about Le Moyne College to build relationships and expand College visibility Conduct off campus interviews during recruiting trips. Engage with local alumni during travel to strengthen relationships and support local enrollment initiatives Represent Le Moyne College at organized off campus recruiting programs including, college nights, national and regional colleges, fairs and mini days. Plan, schedule, and present at Student Information Sessions in targeted geographic areas. (off-campus receptions) Plan, schedule, and present at off campus guidance counselor breakfasts, dinners and association meetings. Participate in panel presentations at secondary schools when invitations are extended to us. Coordinate or assist with other admission related events and programs. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited College or University required. Experience working in an admission office preferred. Valid Driver’s License required. Excellent oral, presentation and written communication skills. Strong organizational skills and time management. Ability to work independently and as a member of a team. Flexibility and willingness to work extended hours during various time periods including evenings and weekends. High level of initiative and imagination. Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish is preferred, but not required. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $24.00 - $27.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Assistant-Director--Admission_JR100326": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Admission",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-17\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Assistant Director is responsible to educate incoming freshman, transfers, parents and counselors about Le Moyne College and the overall college admission process and manage all aspects of college admission including recruitment, counseling, academic advising and evaluation of prospective students and applicants. This position is based at Le Moyne College in Syracuse, NY with a main recruitment territory of Metro NY. This position requires travel to the Metro NY area for student recruitment.  Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Participate as an active member of the professional admission team to design, develop and implement successful marketing and recruitment strategies and plans. Successfully manage assigned primary, secondary and tertiary geographic territories conducting extensive travel to build pipelines, lead recruitment events and expand institutional reach. Counsel, advise and interview prospective first-year and transfer students to guide them through the enrollment lifecycle Evaluate prospective students’ application materials for final recommendations on admission decision. Engage in targeted telemarketing and outreach activities to prospective students and applicants. Lead the organization and execution of on-campus events with the support of the Director of First Year Admission. Plan and host on campus programs for specific student demographics Maximize opportunities regarding the college admission process and access to Le Moyne College by delivering inclusive, culturally sensitive guidance to diverse students, parents and counselors Responsible for specific program responsibilities as assigned by Director (ex: travel coordination, tour guides, etc.) Build, expand, and maintain an internal recruitment database Plans travel and recruitment in the Metro NY area: Visit high schools, junior colleges and multicultural agencies to educate students and counselors about Le Moyne College to build relationships and expand College visibility Conduct off campus interviews during recruiting trips. Engage with local alumni during travel to strengthen relationships and support local enrollment initiatives Represent Le Moyne College at organized off campus recruiting programs including, college nights, national and regional colleges, fairs and mini days. Plan, schedule, and present at Student Information Sessions in targeted geographic areas. (off-campus receptions) Plan, schedule, and present at off campus guidance counselor breakfasts, dinners and association meetings. Participate in panel presentations at secondary schools when invitations are extended to us. Coordinate or assist with other admission related events and programs. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited College or University and 3 years of experience required. Experience working in an admission office preferred. Valid Driver’s License required. Ability to work independently and as a member of a team. Excellent oral, presentation and written communication skills. Strong organizational skills and time management. Flexibility and willingness to work extended hours during various time periods including evenings and weekends. High level of initiative and imagination. Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish is preferred, but not required. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $26.00 - $30.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Senior-Associate-Athletic-Director--External-Affairs_JR100310": {
      "title": "Senior Associate Athletic Director, External Affairs",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-30\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Sr. Associate Athletic Director for External Affairs is a key member of the Athletic leadership team, responsible for the strategic vision, oversight, and execution of all external units within Le Moyne College Athletics. This role is directly accountable for driving departmental revenue, elevating the game-day fan experience, and modernizing sports information and digital media strategies. By unifying corporate partnerships, ticket operations, marketing, and media relations, the Sr. Associate AD ensures a seamless, high-energy fan experience that builds institutional visibility, engages the campus and local communities, and converts fan affinity into long-term financial stability. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Revenue Generation & Strategic Planning (30%) Provide oversight for the identification, solicitation, and closure of new corporate sponsorship agreements Oversee the management of existing partner relationships, ensuring complete contract fulfillment, in-game asset delivery, and multi-year renewals. Provide strategic oversight for the ticket office. Develop and execute aggressive strategies for season, group, mini-plan, and single-game ticket packages to maximize venue capacity and optimize revenue. Explore and establish targets for alternative revenue opportunities, including premium seating, hospitality experiences, merchandise licensing, and digital content monetization. Utilize data analytics and market research to provide regular revenue forecasting, attendance metrics, and strategic performance analysis to the Athletic Director/AVP. Fan Experience & Game Atmosphere Production (30%) Own the overall atmosphere of all home sporting events to ensure a vibrant home-court advantage. Direct and approve all in-game creative elements, music, public address scripts, video board content, and promotional activations. Lead and coordinate game-day stakeholders—including the pep band, cheer/dance squads, spirit groups, and third-party game staff—to maintain a professional, high-energy environment. Collaborate with campus partners to design and execute innovative theme nights, giveaways, and community relations initiatives to increase attendance among students, faculty, staff, and the broader Central New York public. Sports Information, Communications & Brand Development (30%) Oversee and actively contribute to the sports information and communications unit. Direct strategies to build positive relationships with local, regional, and national media to generate national storytelling opportunities. Supervise the coordination of content for the official athletics website and all social media platforms. Establish strict proofing and layer-of-approval processes for public-facing digital materials to ensure strict alignment with college brand standards. Ensure the accurate production of all sports media guides, historical archiving, and live game-day statistics operations. Leadership, Sport Administration & Compliance (10%) Serve on the Athletic Director/AVP’s senior staff, actively contributing to department-wide strategic planning and decision-making. Serve as the designated Sport Administrator for selected athletic programs, providing operational guidance and evaluating head coaches. Maintain strict adherence to and up-to-date knowledge of all NCAA Division I, conference, and institutional rules, regulations, and deadlines. Ensure the physical, emotional, and social welfare of all student-athletes. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Sports Management, Business, Communications, or a related field required; Master’s degree preferred. 7+ years of progressive, full-time experience in sports marketing, revenue generation, or athletic communications, preferably within NCAA Division I athletics. Proven track record of leading, managing, and developing a diverse staff of department area heads, graduate assistants, and interns. Ability to communicate clearly, effectively, and professionally in both written and verbal forms. Proven ability to work constructively and collaboratively within a team environment and across diverse departments. Strong critical thinking skills with the ability to identify issues, propose solutions, and adapt to changing workplace needs. Commitment to fostering an inclusive, respectful, and equitable environment for all colleagues, clients, and stakeholders Ability to work independently, prioritize tasks effectively, and manage multiple projects simultaneously Demonstrated commitment to ethical conduct, honesty, and professional integrity in all workplace interactions Must possess a valid, current U.S. driver’s license. Must have reliable transportation or the ability to rent a vehicle when needed to travel. May need to drive campus vehicles for local events. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range: $70,000 - $75,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Assistant-Director--Alumni-and-Donor-Relations_JR100311": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Alumni and Donor Relations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-26\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Assistant Director for Alumni and Donor Relations plays a vital role in planning and executing signature alumni and donor events, with primary responsibility for the logistics of Reunion Weekend and annual fundraising dinners. In addition, this position assists with athletic alumni programming, manages a small portfolio of corporate and individual prospects and supports the daily administrative operations of the Alumni and Donor Relations team. The role requires excellent organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues, volunteers, and vendors to deliver high-quality experiences that strengthen connections and inspire philanthropy. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Event Management (Primary Focus) Serve as the lead project manager for Reunion Weekends, overseeing logistics, vendor coordination, volunteer support, and event communications. Plan and execute annual fundraising dinners, coordinating with Advancement, Facilities, Catering, and external vendors to deliver high-caliber donor experiences. Assist in the planning and execution of athletic alumni events, working closely with colleagues in Athletics and Advancement. Support other alumni and donor events as needed, including regional gatherings, networking programs, and recognition events. Alumni and Donor Engagement Build strong relationships with alumni volunteers, reunion committees, and event participants. Carry a small portfolio of corporate and individual prospects, engaging them through personalized outreach, event invitations, and stewardship. Assist with donor recognition activities connected to events, including program booklets, signage, and acknowledgments. Team and Administrative Support Provide day-to-day administrative support for the Alumni and Donor Relations team, including budget tracking, event registration management, and database updates. Serve as the point of contact for vendors, alumni inquiries, and internal partners related to event logistics. Contribute to Advancement communications, including event promotions, email campaigns, and website updates Collaboration Partner with colleagues across Advancement and the College to ensure events and engagement initiatives align with institutional priorities. Represent the College at alumni, donor, and campus events, occasionally requiring evening or weekend work. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree required. 3+years of experience in event planning, alumni relations, donor relations, or related fields. Strong organizational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple complex events simultaneously. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong relationship-building skills with alumni, donors, and volunteers. Proficiency with Microsoft Office; experience with event management platforms and advancement databases (e.g., Raiser’s Edge) preferred. Flexibility to work evenings, weekends, and travel for events as needed. Commitment to the College’s Jesuit values of service, excellence, and cura personalis (care for the whole person). Ability to occasional work evenings and weekends. Ability to travel to support alumni and donor events as needed. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $25.00 - $27.50 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Programmer-Analyst_JR100283": {
      "title": "Programmer Analyst",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-02\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Programmer/Analyst is central to maintaining and modernizing the College’s core administrative systems. This position is responsible for the performance, stability, and evolution of our Ellucian Colleague environment while helping transition legacy processes into scalable, modern solutions. The Programmer/Analyst acts as a technical bridge between established systems and emerging technologies—building integrations, reducing technical debt, and enabling more efficient, data-driven operations across the institution. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Maintain and enhance the Ellucian Colleague system and UniData environment to ensure reliability, performance, and data integrity Diagnose and resolve system issues; proactively tune and optimize system performance Develop, modify, and support applications using UniBasic and Envision Create and maintain clear, usable documentation for legacy systems and processes Safeguard sensitive institutional data in alignment with security and compliance standards Reduce technical debt by auditing and streamlining legacy custom code Identify opportunities to replace custom solutions with standard (“baseline”) system functionality Simplify and modernize system architecture to improve maintainability and scalability Decommission obsolete processes, reports, and data structures to support future system upgrades or migrations Design and implement integrations between Colleague and modern platforms (e.g., Canvas, Workday) using APIs, web services (REST/SOAP), and JSON Develop reports and data solutions using tools like SQL Server Reporting Services and Informer Support data exchange processes that enable accurate, timely reporting and decision-making across departments Partner with departments such as Financial Aid, Registrar, and Bursar to align business processes with system capabilities Translate functional needs into technical solutions within the Colleague environment Guide stakeholders through changes that reduce reliance on custom development and improve long-term sustainability Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or equivalent experience required 5+ years of programming experience, ideally in ERP or enterprise systems required Experience with SQL Server or similar relational databases required, experience with Ellucian Colleague, UniData, or UniBasic preferred Familiarity with APIs, web services (REST/SOAP), and JSON required Strong problem-solving skills and ability to translate business requirements into technical solutions Experience with reporting tools such as Informer or SQL Server Reporting Services preferred Familiarity with systems such as Canvas or Workday preferred Experience in higher education or similarly complex institutional environments preferred Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  Pay Range: $70,000 - $75,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Associate-Director--Student-Success_JR100257": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Student Success",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-02-04\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Associate Director of the Student Success Center plays a pivotal role in managing the daily operations of the Center and provides professional support to all Center staff, including professionals and student employees. This position coordinates the tutoring program, collaborates closely with colleagues in the Quantitative Research Center and Writing Center, and empowers students to achieve their academic, personal, and professional goals through individualized coaching and resource connection. In addition, the Associate Director leads and supports retention initiatives by identifying enrollment and persistence risks, coordinating proactive outreach efforts, and collaborating with campus partners to strengthen student retention across all class years. This position will commence no earlier than June 1, 2026. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Center Operations/Management - 30% Oversee the Center’s daily operations such as student programming, academic support services and triage Coordinate programming efforts to support students and create visibility for the Center  Partner with colleagues to develop and implement student success initiatives Respond to inquiries from students, families, faculty, and other college personnel Promote the Center’s resources and achievements to external audiences Work collaboratively with coaches to carry out the mission, goals and outcomes of the Student Success Center Provide staff development, including hiring, mentoring, and evaluation of student staff Carry out logistical duties to support academic advising such as compiling administrative withdrawal data, sending hiatus letters, and reaching out to faculty advisors to provide support Promote and contribute to existing student success efforts while assessing their effectiveness and implementing new initiatives Case Management/Academic Coaching - 25% Provide comprehensive academic coaching to a caseload of students who have been referred. (Referrals may come from Student of Concern reports, faculty referrals, assignments based on academic standing, student-initiated requests, etc.) Engage in initiative-taking management of caseload, including consistent and direct contact with students, and targeted outreach at key points in the semester. Troubleshoot registration, billing and financial aid issues that may arise for students. Assess learner needs in order to help them make fully informed decisions about their pathways as well as challenging them to make progress toward their goals. Develop relationships with identified students that encourage continuation of long-term academic coaching into future semesters, as needed. Assist students in developing self-efficacy by identifying and overcoming obstacles that may be impeding academic success; work with students to learn strong time management and organization skills; motivate students to practice self-regulation and take ownership of their academic success. Engage at-risk students, providing one-on-one intrusive advising meetings to improve engagement and ensure success. Connect students with other campus resources related to tutoring, spiritual support, disability services, counseling and health, housing and food insecurity, career planning, finances, etc. Partner with faculty, academic advisors, and campus colleagues regarding Student of Concern referrals. Assist instructors with follow-up on students who have been referred through the Student of Concern process for excessive absences, unsatisfactory grades, etc. Record applicable interventions via Maxient. Retention Leadership – 20% Monitor early alerts, absences, GPA risk factors, DFW rates, and withdrawal patterns to identify students who may be at risk for attrition. Coordinate campus-wide retention initiatives in partnership with the Director of Student Success and other stakeholders (Dean Restaurant Nights, Registration Fest, Winter and Summer Academic Bridge). Compile the academic standing data (students on warning/probation) and notify undergraduates each semester when they are not in good academic standing Continually refine programing to support students on probation, assign counselors to support them, and provide ongoing training to counselors Lead targeted persistence campaigns focusing on key transition points (e.g., first-year to sophomore retention, post-hiatus return, students on academic warning/probation). Analyze retention and persistence trends to inform programming, resource allocation, and interventions. Collaborate with Academic Deans, Class Deans, Enrollment Management, Financial Aid, Housing, Athletics, and other departments to ensure coordinated outreach and resolution of barriers to persistence. Serve as the Student Success representative on the retention committee Implement best practices for holistic retention support that address academic, social, financial, and wellbeing risk factors. Contribute retention data insights during departmental and campus-wide meetings. Tutoring Oversight - 15% Organize the hiring, supervision, and regular training of student tutors Oversee tutor payroll and monitor the associated budget Coordinate the administration of study groups that are offered in collaboration with various departments and learning communities, including hiring, training, and payroll for peer leaders, and maintaining records on all group sessions/workshops Continually seek faculty input on tutoring effectiveness and operations Serve as a liaison to other Le Moyne College programs (i.e., the Physician Assistant program, nursing partnerships, etc.) regarding academic support issues and scheduling Maintain tutoring data and provide regular reports and assessments Professional Development - 5% Meet regularly with the Director of Student Success to discuss the status of retention data/efforts. Participate as an active member of the Student Success Center staff meetings and retreats and provide informed feedback and initiative. Serve as a member of key campus committees related to student success Attend division- and campus-wide meetings to keep current on college initiatives, student demographics, program offerings, upcoming trends, etc. Continually review best practices related to student success and relay pertinent information to campus partners as needed. Manage confidential student information with tact, discretion, and in compliance with FERPA regulations Progress Monitoring – 5% Develop and maintain accurate, organized, and detailed student records of students who have sought assistance. Create and maintain student plans in close collaboration with the Director of the Student Success Center to ensure accurate counseling, mitigation of student issues, and ongoing feedback; adjust strategies as needed. Monitor student academic progress by compiling, analyzing, and reporting on student progress utilizing available databases and resources (e.g., Phinfo, Datatel, Informer, WCOnline, CampusGroups) Assess student attrition risk and vulnerability and intervene at critical points of the student's educational path. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s Degree and 5+ years of relevant experience is required or equivalent experience and education. Master’s degree in Higher Education, Counseling, Education or related field is preferred. Establish and maintain cooperative and productive relationships with both campus and off-campus contacts, including students, faculty, prospects, parents, and community partners Possess excellent interpersonal and written communication skills Maintain a high level of confidentiality due to the sensitivity of the nature of the student and college information this position requires Experience working directly with college students, preferably with transfer, non-traditional, and/or under-represented student populations, concerning academic success Experience with large- and small-scale event planning Experience with Microsoft Office, Datatel Student Management Software, and familiarity with Course Management Software (e.g. Canvas), Informer, and Slate are preferred Willingness to work evenings and weekends to accommodate student needs and programming Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment Excellent customer service skills Strong written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated time management and organization skills. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $62,354 - $66,500 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Associate-Director--Annual-Giving_JR100254": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Annual Giving",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-01-20\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Associate Director of Annual Giving plays a key role in the planning, execution, and management of strategies that drive philanthropic support through annual giving programs. This position focuses on donor acquisition, retention, and upgrading, as well as strengthening engagement among alumni, parents, faculty, staff, and friends of the College. The Associate Director partners closely with colleagues in Advancement, particularly with the Engagement Center, and Marketing and Communications to design multi-channel campaigns that inspire giving and align with institutional priorities. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Support the development and implementation of a comprehensive annual giving plan to achieve participation and revenue goals. Oversee key components of the annual giving program, including direct mail, email, texting, digital campaigns, crowdfunding, and Giving Day. Review giving data and trends to inform segmentation, messaging, and campaign strategies. Collaborate with the Advancement team to identify new opportunities for donor engagement and pipeline growth. Manage a portfolio of annual donors and prospects to cultivate, solicit, and steward gifts Partner with Alumni and Donor Relations to ensure execution of stewardship plans that recognize annual giving donors at all levels. Partner with Alumni and Donor Relations team to integrate giving opportunities into campus and regional events. Supervise and mentor staff, students, and/or volunteers engaged in annual giving efforts. Collaborate across Advancement to ensure consistency and coordination in fundraising messages and donor experiences. Track and report on campaign performance, donor retention, participation rates, and other key metrics. Maintain accurate records in the Raiser’s Edge and GiveCampus CRM systems. Use data to identify trends, test new strategies, and inform long-term planning. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree required. 5+ years of experience in fundraising, annual giving, or related field required, experience in higher education preferred. Demonstrated success managing campaigns or projects from conception through completion. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong analytical skills with experience using data to drive decisions. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Excellent customer service skills. Ability to work independently but collaboratively as part of a goal-oriented team. Commitment to the Jesuit mission and values of the College. Familiarity with CRM systems and fundraising software (e.g., Raiser’s Edge, GiveCampus) preferred. Understanding of donor segmentation and digital fundraising techniques preferred. Supervisory and/or volunteer management experience preferred. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $63,000 - $73,500 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Community-Health-and-Wellness-Program-Specialist_JR100369": {
      "title": "Community Health and Wellness Program Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. Position Summary                                                                            The Community Health and Wellness Program Specialist is responsible for planning, implementing, and evaluating community-based programs that promote healthy aging, independence, wellness, and fall prevention for older adults. This position provides evidence-informed fall prevention programming, exercise and education, participant screening and functional assessments within the employee’s training and scope of practice, and wellness interventions while collaborating with community organizations throughout Central New York. The Community Health and Wellness Program Specialist assists with program development, participant outcome measurement, data management, community outreach, and social media engagement to support CARE's mission of improving the health, safety, and quality of life of older adults. This is a part time position working 20-25 hours per week. The position includes a combination of in person work at Le Moyne College and community program sites and remote work for appropriate administrative, planning, data, outreach, and social media responsibilities. This position is funded by external sources and is contingent on the continued receipt of those funds. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Fall Prevention and Community Wellness  Deliver CARE fall prevention, healthy aging, wellness, and exercise programming for older adults in community-based settings.  Lead group exercise and educational components in a safe, engaging, and age-appropriate manner and adapt activities to participant abilities and established program protocols. Complete participant screenings and standardized functional measures within the employee’s education, credentials, training, and scope of practice; identify concerns that require referral to an appropriate licensed healthcare professional.  Provide education related to fall-risk reduction, home safety, mobility, healthy aging, assistive devices, caregiver strategies, and other wellness topics consistent with training and professional scope.  Assist with the development and implementation of CARE programs, workshops, presentations, and community initiatives.   Community Partnerships and Outreach  Develop and maintain positive working relationships with community partners, older adults, caregivers, healthcare organizations, and agencies serving older adults.  Assist with outreach to identify new program sites, partnership opportunities, presentations, community events, and referral relationships.  Represent CARE and Le Moyne College professionally at community programs, meetings, health fairs, and outreach events.    Social Media and Digital Outreach  Assist with and maintain CARE's social media presence as a required responsibility of the position. Create, schedule, and post program updates, educational content, event promotion, participant highlights, and community outreach content on CARE's approved social media platforms. Assist with basic content creation using Canva or similar tools and coordinate photographs, graphics, captions, and program information in accordance with CARE and Le Moyne College policies.    Data Management and Program Evaluation  Collect, maintain, and assist with analysis of participant and program data, ensuring timely and accurate entry into required tracking systems.  Support outcome measurement and reporting for funders, community partners, and organizational leadership.  Assist with preparation of program metrics, summaries, presentations, and grant-related reports that demonstrate program reach and impact.  Maintain participant confidentiality and follow applicable organizational policies and data-security practices.   General Responsibilities  Participate in required meetings, training, and professional development activities. Collaborate effectively with CARE staff, Le Moyne College departments, students, community partners, and interdisciplinary professionals.  Demonstrate professionalism, reliability, sound judgment, initiative, integrity, and respect for the dignity of all participants.  Perform other duties related to CARE programming and community health initiatives as assigned. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required: Experience working with older adults in a wellness, healthcare, rehabilitation, or community setting. Background in movement, health, rehabilitation support, or therapeutic instruction (e.g., group fitness, senior fitness certifications, kinesiology/exercise science application, physical/occupational therapy support) Strong communication and interpersonal skills and the ability to work effectively with older adults and community partners.  Comfort with basic technology and digital tools, including Microsoft Office, Zoom, Canva, Instagram, Facebook, and/or similar platforms.  Ability and willingness to create and manage social media content as an ongoing responsibility of the position.  Strong organizational skills and ability to work independently in both in-person and remote settings. Reliable transportation and ability to travel to community program sites throughout Central New York. Preferred: Graduate degree in either Physical Therapy or Occupational Therapy and a current license in NYS OR a degree/certification in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Gerontology, Public Health, Health Coaching, or wellness-related fields. For applicants working under a licensed or certified healthcare profession, current New York State licensure/certification and good standing are required when applicable to the duties performed. Experience working with older adults, fall prevention, balance and mobility, community wellness, rehabilitation, or chronic disease prevention. Experience with program coordination, community outreach, data collection, outcome tracking, or grant-funded initiatives. Relevant certifications or training in evidence-based fall prevention, older-adult fitness, or wellness programming Working Conditions and Physical Demands Our campus thrives on the energy, collaboration, and shared ideas of our community. We believe that the best student mentorship, professional growth, and creative breakthroughs happen through real-time, face-to-face connection. To support this vibrant academic environment, positions at Le Moyne College are based on-campus. This ensures our teams can seamlessly collaborate, build strong professional relationships, and directly contribute to our student-centered mission. Additional Information: Pay Range:  $30.00 - $38.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Coordinator--Keenan-Center_JR100367": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Keenan Center",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. Position Summary The Keenan Center’s mission is to increase the density of entrepreneurial, innovative and creative talent in Central New York. The Office Coordinator for the Keenan Center for Entrepreneurship, Innovation, and Creativity will provide administrative support for the Center.  This position will support the Keenan Center’s operations across all of its entrepreneurial, innovative and creative efforts. This includes supporting its various programs (e.g., drone, project based learning, entrepreneurship, multiple campus and community events, etc.), assisting in the management of our highly engaged team of  student workers and serving as a main point of contact for site partners and vendors. This position is funded by external sources and is contingent on the continued receival of those funds. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position:  Coordinate, schedule and recruit for year-round programming involving K - 12 youth, community members and partnering organizations. Coordinate logistics for Keenan Center events, including venue booking, guest invitations, and on-site support. Assist in the management of day-to-day operations, including scheduling meetings, managing calendars, and handling correspondence. Assist with consumables, inventory and general maker space management. Assist in completing administrative requirements and coordinating deadlines with staff members. Assist in the designing and distribution of e-mail newsletters and promotional materials for in-house and partner organizations.  Maintain records of client/partner meetings and Keenan Center visitors. Maintain the customer relationship management (CRM) system and contacts, ensuring data accuracy for effective communication and outreach. Assist with lists, contracts, and fundraising workflow Assist in managing budgetary and financial tasks, such as tracking expenses, processing invoices, and reconciling accounts. Assist in developing and deploying marketing initiatives that target alums, industry partners, and prospective contacts as well as responding to recipients' calls to action Notify industry partners of engagement opportunities, coordinate responses with career services, and, in some cases, directly with students and schedule events as needed  Ensure compliance with organizational policies and procedures, including data privacy regulations, record retention policies, and ethical guidelines. Assist in the development and implementation of Keenan Center policies and procedures for new and existing programs. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Strong interest in working within a mission driven environment that is highly collaborative and curious.  Possess strong time management, interpersonal, communication and leadership skills. Proven ability to plan and act strategically, tactically and creatively. Be comfortable in a team setting and able to work successfully with senior administrators, faculty members and key volunteers. Be self-sufficient and reliable, and stay up-to-date if and when working from home. Proven record as a self-starter, builder and initiator of constant process improvement.  Demonstrated ability to learn, navigate and work comfortably with various technology platforms. Experience with our willingness and aptitude to learn web-based content management systems. Ability to collaborate effectively within a team environment, managing relationships internally and externally, Experience or ability to work across diverse cultures and communicate effectively with global clients.  Working Conditions and Physical Demands Our campus thrives on the energy, collaboration, and shared ideas of our community. We believe that the best student mentorship, professional growth, and creative breakthroughs happen through real-time, face-to-face connection. To support this vibrant academic environment, positions at Le Moyne College are based on-campus. This ensures our teams can seamlessly collaborate, build strong professional relationships, and directly contribute to our student-centered mission. Additional Information: Pay Range:  $20.00 - $24.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Director--Colvin-Center_JR100363": {
      "title": "Director, Colvin Center",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. The Ruth Colvin Adult Learning Center has been established to offer flexible, learner-centered programming that supports diverse goals, including foundational skill building, English language acquisition, workforce readiness, and digital literacy. This instruction will be delivered through a mix of classes, small-group learning, and one-on-one tutoring. The Center will also provide online remote GED instruction via consistent, data-driven small group tutoring that will allow for flexible scheduling to help learners strengthen reading and math skills while progressing toward GED attainment. Beyond instruction, the Center will function as a connector—linking learners to college pathways, workforce training, community organizations, and social supports.   ProLiteracy, the nation’s largest adult literacy and basic education organization, is providing strategic guidance and capacity-building support to help establish the Center and strengthen its leadership, operations, and programming as it evolves and broadens its reach. Position Summary                                                                         The Ruth Colvin Center Director will develop and guide the Center’s mission of empowering adults by providing accessible, high-quality literacy instruction that opens pathways to further education, meaningful employment, and full participation in civic and community life. The Director will work to advance the Center’s long-term vision of building a community where every adult can read, write, and communicate with confidence, thus unlocking lifelong learning and economic opportunity.   The Director will be an effective, compassionate individual who is prepared to work with linguistically and culturally diverse client populations and adults with literacy challenges to lead the Center in achieving its goals. This is a 12-month, full time position and may include evening and weekend hours based on operational needs. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Direct the Center’s student services by providing design and oversight of the following areas: Student recruitment and waitlist management (including collaborating with the Le Moyne Communication Office and the Bosch Academy Director as necessary to develop marketing materials, social media efforts, and in-person events to recruit students and developing relationships with referral organizations across the community) Student intake (including designing and facilitating an intake process that includes assessment, data collection, and personalized learning plan development) Instruction (including selecting curricula, purchasing instructional materials, maintaining learning area and facilities, and teaching classes and/or tutoring literacy as a substitute or back-up instructor as necessary) Student progress (including collecting and monitoring student learning data and conducting oversight of student learning plans) Student support (including managing the support services students need to overcome learning barriers such as transportation, child care, work schedules, etc.) Student involvement (including developing ways for students to be active stakeholders in the Center) Support the Center’s instructors by providing design and oversight of the following areas: Instructor recruitment (including developing marketing materials, social media efforts, and in-person events as necessary to recruit instructors in collaboration with referral organizations across the community) Instructor intake (including designing and facilitating an application and intake process that includes reviewing volunteer applicants, making decisions about volunteer viability, collecting data about scheduling availability and interest, and organizing schedules) Instructor training (including initial/preservice training and ongoing/in-service professional development and support) Instructor support and supervision (including and maintaining a system of monitoring, supporting, and evaluating instructors) Provide organization and administrative oversight by: Monitoring and assessing scope and effectiveness of existing services on a continuing basis Making decisions about the Center’s staffing, curriculum, and direction Making recommendations to Bosch Academy leadership regarding program changes Overseeing the Center’s budget Ordering supplies as necessary Maintaining the Center’s learning area(s) and technological equipment Submitting an annual report to Bosch Academy leadership and other interested parties Establishing and maintaining community relationships to facilitate needed support for the organization: i.e., volunteers, students, community partners for recruitment purposes Maintaining a positive and effective relationship with other literacy service providers in Syracuse and the surrounding area Establishing relationships with state and national literacy organizations Updating and maintaining web and social media presences Promoting the Center through personal and media contacts Maintaining effective working relationships with students, volunteers, donors, and other stakeholders through technology or in person Speaking to donors and community members Planning and facilitating public relations events and publicity campaigns Providing additional administrative support as necessary Stay abreast of the latest trends and research in literacy education through ongoing professional development.   Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required: Master’s Degree in adult education, nonprofit management, or other related field (applied linguistics, comparative or contrastive rhetoric, curriculum and instruction, education, second language acquisition, TESOL, etc.) Minimum 3-5 years managerial experience in adult literacy education or similarly focused nonprofit organization Proven commitment to understanding and responding to the needs of adult learners, especially related to Adult Basic Education (ABE) Experience teaching literacy to English language learners and understanding the communication needs of culturally and linguistically diverse learners Equivalent combination of education and experience will be considered Working Conditions and Physical Demands Our campus thrives on the energy, collaboration, and shared ideas of our community. We believe that the best student mentorship, professional growth, and creative breakthroughs happen through real-time, face-to-face connection. To support this vibrant academic environment, positions at Le Moyne College are based on-campus. This ensures our teams can seamlessly collaborate, build strong professional relationships, and directly contribute to our student-centered mission. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $63,000 - $70,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Associate-Director--Career-Advising-and-Development_JR100362-1": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Career Advising and Development",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Associate Director of Career Advising is responsible for leadership, management and implementation of the College’s Internship, Mentorship, and Ignite Fellowship programs in close collaboration and coordination with the divisions of Academic Affairs, Enrollment Management and Institutional Advancement. Additionally, the Associate Director develops academically based career programming in the form of workshops, practicum classes, Promise Program, Career Conversations, and collaborations with campus faculty. This is an administrative, ten-month, full-time position that runs from August 1st through May 31st .   PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Collaborate with faculty internship coordinators and local, regional, national and international employers in order to increase internship and career opportunities for our students and alumni Collect, record and track data on internship activity across the institution in order to produce reports that outline the results of our efforts and their impact on our students. Share internship resources for students, faculty, staff and other college stakeholders through the website, emails, and online opportunities platform (Handshake). Develop and disseminate institutional procedures for best practice internships including resources for sample forms, intern evaluations and learning agreements. Provide professional internship and career advising to individual students and groups at all stages of the career discernment process. Lead outreach efforts to students, faculty and on-campus organizations that inform and encourage participation in office programs and events. Collaborate in the implementation of annual career events including internship and career fairs, on-campus recruiting, “success” and graduate school preparation programs. Oversee the Ignite Fellowship program, an alumni-funded group of fellowships that support students’ internship or research experiences over the summer Collaborate with the office of Alumni and Parent Programs to increase engagement between current students and alumni, specifically the Career Conversations program. Coordinate the annual Faculty Career Mentor Awards recognizing outstanding contributions from faculty across the College Teach two 1 credit practicum courses focused on career exploration and networking utilizing Designing Your Life techniques Oversee the Career Student Ambassador program including recruiting, training, and supervision of 3-5 students Serve as a liaison to science academic departments and select athletic teams Assist in the marketing and outreach efforts for events coordinated and executed through the office. Represent the office at university-wide events including but not limited to admissions open houses and new and transfer student orientations. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree At least 4 years of related experience Evidence of leadership skills and excellence in the areas of team building and community relations. Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast- paced environment. Willingness to take initiative being innovative and creative in working with a variety of constituents including students, employers, faculty. alumni and parents. Master's degree in counseling, higher education, social welfare, or a related area or similar related work experience preferred. Demonstrated familiarity with the internship and employment recruitment process preferred. Administrative experience with Handshake or a similar customer relationship management platform preferred. Knowledge of college student development and experience advising undergraduate students, graduate students, and alumni preferred. Working Conditions and Physical Demands Our campus thrives on the energy, collaboration, and shared ideas of our community. We believe that the best student mentorship, professional growth, and creative breakthroughs happen through real-time, face-to-face connection. To support this vibrant academic environment, positions at Le Moyne College are based on-campus. This ensures our teams can seamlessly collaborate, build strong professional relationships, and directly contribute to our student-centered mission. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $ 53,000 - $56,500 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    }
  },
